== 7.6 Chapter 7 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Working capital is],
  [total assets less total liabilities],
  [current assets less current liabilities],
  [fixed assets less current liabilities],
  [share capital plus reserves]
)

#mcq(2, [Which is a fixed asset?],
  [delivery van],
  [stock],
  [debtors],
  [cash at bank]
)

#mcq(3, [Which is a current liability?],
  [bank loan repayable in five years],
  [trade creditors],
  [premises],
  [motor vehicle]
)

#mcq(4, [If current assets are ₦3.2m and current liabilities ₦1.4m, working capital is],
  [₦4.6m],
  [₦3.2m],
  [₦1.8m],
  [₦1.4m]
)

#mcq(5, [A business with current assets of ₦3.2m and current liabilities of ₦3.0m has],
  [negative working capital],
  [comfortable working capital],
  [a current ratio of about 1.07 and little cushion],
  [no current assets]
)

#mcq(6, [Which source of finance is short-term?],
  [a mortgage],
  [an ordinary share issue],
  [a ten-year debenture],
  [trade credit]
)

#mcq(7, [Which source is long-term?],
  [debenture],
  [trade credit],
  [bank overdraft],
  [accrued wages]
)

#mcq(8, [A bank overdraft is],
  [a short-term facility allowing a negative balance],
  [a share issue],
  [a long-term loan],
  [a grant]
)

#mcq(9, [The cheapest internal source of finance is],
  [a debenture],
  [a share issue],
  [a bank loan],
  [retained profit]
)

#mcq(10, [Ploughed-back profit is also called],
  [reserve capital],
  [retained earnings],
  [dividend],
  [share premium]
)

#mcq(11, [Leasing is attractive because it],
  [avoids a large capital outlay],
  [has no cost],
  [transfers ownership at once],
  [increases share capital]
)

#mcq(12, [The stock exchange's main function for a company is],
  [to insure it],
  [to lend it money],
  [to provide a market in its shares],
  [to collect its tax]
)

#mcq(13, [A stock exchange also],
  [regulates companies],
  [fixes the price of goods],
  [mobilises savings for investment],
  [prints currency]
)

#mcq(14, [A bull expects prices to],
  [rise],
  [fall],
  [stay flat],
  [be fixed]
)

#mcq(15, [A bear expects prices to],
  [rise],
  [fall],
  [stay flat],
  [double]
)

#mcq(16, [The first document in a business transaction by correspondence is the],
  [letter of enquiry],
  [credit note],
  [invoice],
  [receipt]
)

#mcq(17, [A quotation states],
  [the goods already delivered],
  [the profit made],
  [the tax due],
  [the price and terms on which the seller will supply]
)

#mcq(18, [An order becomes a contract when],
  [it is posted],
  [the goods are paid for],
  [it is accepted by the seller],
  [the invoice is sent]
)

#mcq(19, [A delivery note is signed by],
  [the tax office],
  [the bank],
  [the seller alone],
  [the buyer or his agent on receipt]
)

#mcq(20, [An invoice is sent by],
  [the carrier to the buyer],
  [the bank to the seller],
  [the buyer to the seller],
  [the seller to the buyer]
)

#mcq(21, [A credit note is issued by the seller when],
  [a discount is refused],
  [goods are returned or an overcharge is corrected],
  [payment is late],
  [goods are sold on credit]
)

#mcq(22, [A debit note is issued by],
  [the bank],
  [the carrier],
  [the buyer],
  [the seller]
)

#mcq(23, [A statement of account is sent],
  [daily],
  [at the end of a period, listing all transactions],
  [only when there is a dispute],
  [by the buyer]
)

#mcq(24, [A receipt is evidence that],
  [goods were ordered],
  [money has been paid],
  [goods were manufactured],
  [a discount was offered]
)

#mcq(25, [E.&O.E. on an invoice means],
  [errors and omissions excepted],
  [export and other expenses],
  [everything ordered exactly],
  [each order entered]
)

#mcq(26, [Goods listed at ₦50,000 are subject to 20% and then 5% trade discount. The net price is],
  [₦38,000],
  [₦47,500],
  [₦40,000],
  [₦37,500]
)

#mcq(27, [In the question above, the total trade discount allowed is],
  [₦10,000],
  [₦15,000],
  [₦13,750],
  [₦12,000]
)

#mcq(28, [A chain of discounts of 20% then 5% is equivalent to a single discount of],
  [25%],
  [22%],
  [24%],
  [23%]
)

#mcq(29, [Trade discount is recorded in the ledger],
  [as a discount received],
  [not at all — it is deducted before entry],
  [as a discount allowed],
  [as an expense]
)

#mcq(30, [Cash discount is recorded because it],
  [is not a real discount],
  [changes the amount actually paid],
  [is a tax],
  [is given before the sale]
)

#mcq(31, [Capital employed equals],
  [total liabilities],
  [fixed assets plus working capital],
  [current assets minus stock],
  [share capital only]
)

#mcq(32, [Which is NOT a source of business finance?],
  [bank loan],
  [debenture],
  [trade credit],
  [sales tax collected]
)

#mcq(33, [A mortgage is a loan secured on],
  [land or buildings],
  [debtors],
  [cash],
  [stock]
)

#mcq(34, [The main risk of relying on an overdraft is that it is],
  [long-term],
  [unsecured by definition],
  [repayable on demand],
  [expensive to arrange]
)

#mcq(35, [Which document would a buyer consult to check what he owes at the end of the month?],
  [quotation],
  [statement of account],
  [delivery note],
  [enquiry]
)

#mcq(36, [A proforma invoice is used to],
  [record a return],
  [acknowledge payment],
  [show the price before an order is placed],
  [claim payment]
)

#mcq(37, [The working capital cycle begins with],
  [sales and ends with purchases],
  [stock and ends with stock],
  [cash and ends with cash],
  [credit and ends with cash]
)

#mcq(38, [If a firm's current ratio falls from 2:1 to 1.2:1, its liquidity has],
  [deteriorated],
  [improved],
  [become negative],
  [stayed the same]
)

#mcq(39, [A buyer who believes a reduction is due but has not been allowed it issues a],
  [debit note],
  [receipt],
  [credit note],
  [statement]
)

#mcq(40, [Share capital raised above nominal value creates],
  [a liability],
  [a debenture],
  [a share premium],
  [a dividend]
)

