  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    A fixed asset is held for use in the business, not for resale.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Creditors fall due within a year and are settled from current assets.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    3.2 − 1.4 = 1.8 million naira.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The ratio is barely above one, so a small fall in stock would cause a squeeze.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Trade credit is repaid in weeks or months.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    A debenture typically runs for many years.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It is repayable on demand, which makes it short-term and flexible.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    No interest or issue cost is paid on profit kept in the business.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It is profit kept in the business rather than distributed.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The firm pays for use rather than ownership.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It gives shareholders liquidity, which makes them willing to subscribe.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It channels household savings into productive enterprise.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The bull buys now to sell later at a higher price.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The bear sells now, expecting to buy back cheaper.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The buyer asks what is available and on what terms.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    It is the seller's offer, which the buyer's order may accept.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    Acceptance is what turns an offer into an agreement.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
    The signature proves that the goods listed were received.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.94pt)[
